#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Inspect and edit Drawy boards (.drawy: one zstd frame of compact JSON)
# without opening Drawy: dump, render, check, unpack/pack, and edits
# that Drawy loads the same as its own.
#
# Item rects, text sizes and drops come from drawy-render, which links
# the installed libdrawygui. It is built on demand from
# ../share/drawyctl/render.cpp into ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/drawyctl
# against the Drawy source clone at the installed tag (DRAWY_SRC,
# default ~/projects/upstream/drawy). DRAWYCTL_RENDER names a prebuilt
# renderer instead. FREEFORM boxes assume Drawy's default Pressure
# Sensitivity: drawy-render never reads drawyrc.
#
# Every write is decoded again, validated and rendered before an atomic
# replace; an existing target is first copied to .../drawyctl/backups.
# Drawy never re-reads a board: see WRITTEN_NOTE.
# Drawy ignores GROUP properties and zorder on load: the array order is
# the stacking order.
# `drawyctl selftest` runs every command on a synthetic board.
# Citations are file:line under src/ in the Drawy source at the tag.

